# ThinkTech Storage API - manual tests (Visual Studio / Rider / VS Code REST Client)
# Start the API with the "http" launch profile first.
# The secrets below belong to the DEVELOPMENT-ONLY clients in appsettings.json (not published to the server).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5059
@clientId = dev-console
@clientSecret = bLK4ui1dm5qjj9gyjSTEW7caTGQTFSZVf4AXqTMVQO8
@readOnlyClientId = dev-readonly
@readOnlyClientSecret = rLFXIC8D00ve9B3XUrUf8Kh5At5_JL1Y85fflIdiFjY

### Health (anonymous)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 1. Authenticate: client id + secret -> access token (JSON)
# @name token
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientId": "{{clientId}}",
  "clientSecret": "{{clientSecret}}"
}

### 1b. Authenticate: standard OAuth 2.0 client_credentials form
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id={{clientId}}&client_secret={{clientSecret}}

### 2. Upload
# @name upload
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/files
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=ThinkTechBoundary

--ThinkTechBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="invoice-1001.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

Hello from the ThinkTech Storage API.
--ThinkTechBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="category"

invoices
--ThinkTechBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="referenceId"

INV-1001
--ThinkTechBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="metadata"

{"customer":"ACME Ltd","branch":"Dhaka"}
--ThinkTechBoundary--

### 3. Metadata
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/files/{{upload.response.body.$.id}}/metadata
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 4. Download
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/files/{{upload.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}

### 5. Delete
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/files/{{upload.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
